NAME
    esde-check - load ES-DE themes for every variant and system and measure them as TSV

SYNOPSIS
    esde-check [--diagnostics | --properties] [--systems a,b,...] <folder>...

DESCRIPTION
    The development tool of the emusen.dev module for the Qt front end's
    ES-DE engine (EmuSen_Qt.md §4.4): the corpus measure of ES-DE themes,
    over the check module of the emusen-esde crate at Frontend/esde. Each
    <folder> is a theme (it holds capabilities.xml, or its first subfolder
    does) or a corpus, a folder whose subfolders are themes. Each theme is
    loaded by the engine's loader once for every selectable variant (or
    once when it offers none) and every system, at 1280 x 800 with the
    other choices automatic, as pass 3's survey loaded them
    (EmuSen_BigPicture.md §25.8). The systems are EmuSen's five, nes,
    snes, gb, gbc and n64, unless --systems names others; a system is
    loaded under its short name as its folder, name and full name.

    The output is TSV with a header line. By default it is one row a
    theme:

        theme        the folder's name
        loads        yes when every system is themed by some variant
        systems      the systems themed, of those asked for
        variants     the selectable variants (1 when none is offered)
        runs         the loads made: variants times systems
        errors       errors over all the runs (each unthemes a system)
        warnings     warnings over all the runs
        set          the type.property pairs the theme sets, in any run,
                     drawn or accepted
        unknown      those the loader does not know (an error)
        unsupported  those the scene and its painter do not draw
        whole        yes when it loads with nothing unknown or
                     unsupported and no undrawn kind
        kinds        the element kinds used
        undrawn      kinds not drawn, and carousel:<type> for a wheel
                     carousel, which is drawn only in part

    and a last line '# N themes, N load, N drawn whole, N use no
    undrawn kind': the three headline numbers of EmuSen_Qt.md §4.4.

    --diagnostics prints each distinct diagnostic at warning or above
    instead, a row each: theme, severity, code, file (relative to the
    theme), line and message. Severities and codes are the loader's
    (EmuSen_BigPicture.md §12.3).

    --properties prints the property map instead, a row a pair: theme,
    type.property and its state, one of set (drawn or accepted),
    unsupported or unknown. The scene's table,
    Frontend/esde/src/scene/mapping.tsv, lists every pair once as drawn,
    accepted (no visible effect in EmuSen, such as the help bar's dimmed
    set) or later:<family>; the painter's stages move pairs to drawn.

    Nothing is fetched: the corpus is fetched beforehand, outside the
    repository (EmuSen_Qt.md §4.5.4), and the command only reads it.

EXIT STATUS
    0 when every theme loads, 1 when one or more does not, 2 when it
    could not run (a folder missing, an option unknown).

EXAMPLES
    esde-check ~/.cache/emusen/bigpicture/corpus/xml
    esde-check --diagnostics ~/.cache/emusen/bigpicture/corpus/xml/caralt-es-de
    esde-check --properties --systems snes ~/themes/art-book-next-es-de

SEE ALSO
    qml-rules(1), dupes(1); EmuSen_Qt.md §4.4 and §4.5;
    EmuSen_BigPicture.md §12, §25.8, §31 and §35; the corpus measures
    committed under Testing/esde-corpus/.
